  "ingredients": [
    "9 New Mexico dry chiles - washed, with stems and seeds removed",
    "3 cups water",
    "5 pounds boneless beef chuck roast, trimmed of fat",
    "0.5 cup all-purpose flour",
    "1 tablespoon kosher salt",
    "1 tablespoon black pepper",
    "3 tablespoons olive oil",
    "1 large yellow onion, chopped",
    "2 cups beef stock, or as needed"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Gather all ingredients.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/hNtAQvWjLjGmi2qG0HOp5auL3-A=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/45386-chile-colorado-DDMFS-step-1-BG-1270-debd60fccf7c4bffa2963cfb707496b8.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/45386/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Place chiles and 3 cups water into a medium stockpot, and bring to a boil. Remove from heat and steep for 30 minutes to soften.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/SHRx6ZKWiNnaYgjpo5gsK6Ixt9Y=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/45386-chile-colorado-DDMFS-step-2-BG-1280-e617afca5baa46c19d2cf5b1455db25f.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/45386/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Strain into a bowl, reserving the cooking liquid.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/4SU8g0CXWlSruVS4McQfE7knlbA=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/45386-chile-colorado-DDMFS-step-3-BG-1309-58a2208a84174bb381d2ffb46ff140c7.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/45386/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Place chiles and some of the liquid into a blender, and purée until smooth. Add more liquid as necessary to form a smooth sauce.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/ivBsRA8ARvc-T4UlLCiaJEXUivc=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/45386-chile-colorado-DDMFS-step-4-BG-1319-e6d581b84e0c41a4939f5716ecc43e8b.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/45386/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pass sauce through a fine mesh strainer to remove any seeds or tough skins; set aside.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/vfvyrFpGYJ_7rtJy8NPceLQj7ZI=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/45386-chile-colorado-DDMFS-step-5-BG-1322-253936a975464b5e8f4bee9db0b83235.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/45386/step_05.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cut beef into 1- to 2-inch chunks. Combine flour, salt, and pepper in a medium bowl. Dredge beef chunks in the seasoned flour; set aside.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/Gze5p3zDaxf7tYl45PucmISXIEI=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/45386-chile-colorado-DDMFS-step-7-BG-1293-ddba8dafd62243f1893c94d2b3106140.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/45386/step_06.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Heat olive oil in a large pot over medium heat. Sauté onion until tender and translucent, about 5 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/Or6l03UkUZyq98v_7trddJomszU=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/45386-chile-colorado-DDMFS-step-8-BG-1302-ee50a78d7a4741fea9428b45c300962d.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/45386/step_07.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add beef chunks a few at a time, so as not to overcrowd the pot, and cook until evenly brown. Remove seared meat, and continue browning the remaining meat. Return reserved seared meat to the pot.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/6WTbK7BDejJtRkC62mCG3sQGw48=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/45386-chile-colorado-DDMFS-step-9-BG-1307-8425e2ec001e48fcbc7c412730827b9c.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/45386/step_08.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Stir in puréed chile mixture. Add beef stock just to cover beef chunks, or to personal preference. Bring to a boil over medium heat. Reduce heat to lowest setting, and simmer for 3 hours, or until meat is tender. If necessary, adjust with more stock during cooking.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/bVb9g07hFGqLIDk2aPnZhhIhlVU=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/45386-chile-colorado-DDMFS-step-10-BG-1333-b49a44a6bb774330b2de2a120a9c447b.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/45386/step_09.webp"
    }
  ],
